/target
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.DS_Store
/bee-sync/

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# secrets and local data — never track these even if they wander in
*.key
*.env
.env
config.toml
docs/OPERATIONS.md
docs/EMBEDDING-EXAMPLES.md

# The gold eval sets: queries mined from real episodes. They live at
# ~/.mecha-graph/eval/ now, and this is the belt to that braces.
#
# **The export used to be what stood between these and the world**, and it
# stripped them by name. Working in this repo directly removes it, so a
# stale private working copy carried forward — or a re-run of
# build-semantic-gold.py — puts them back inside the checkout where
# `git add -A` will stage them. Neither gate would object: a query like
# "when did I last meet <someone>" contains no roster term, so the hook and
# CI both pass clean, and a force-push is not a delete.
#
# eval/synthetic/gold.jsonl is the fictional set and is deliberately
# tracked; neither pattern below matches it.
eval/gold.jsonl
eval/gold-semantic.jsonl

# The tooling that produces and reads those sets, which docs still name by
# repo-relative path. Same reasoning: the files themselves are clean, but a
# path that resolves inside the checkout is a path something will stage.
scripts/build-semantic-gold.py
scripts/score-semantic.py
scripts/diagnose-failures.py
/.claude/
